{"shortDescription":"RNS Number : 6352W  Kendrick Resources PLC  29 September 2026   29 September 2026Kendrick Resources Plc(\"Kendrick\" or \"the Company\")Teufelskuppe Delivers Compelling New Drill ResultsExcellent pXRF Results Achieved for Both the Diamond and Reverse Circulation Drilling ProgrammesKendrick Resources Pl…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":["RNS Number : 6352W  Kendrick Resources PLC  29 September 2026   ",{"type":"p","children":["29 September 2026"]},{"type":"p","children":["Kendrick Resources Plc"]},{"type":"p","children":["(\"Kendrick\" or \"the Company\")"]},{"type":"p","children":["Teufelskuppe Delivers Compelling New Drill Results"]},{"type":"p","children":["Excellent pXRF Results Achieved for Both the Diamond and Reverse Circulation Drilling Programmes"]},{"type":"p","children":["Kendrick Resources Plc is pleased to announce an update on the Teufelskuppe (\"TK\") project.  A total of 90 drill holes have been completed to date, 38 diamond and 52 reverse circulation (\"RC\") drill holes. Detailed logging and sampling are ongoing with sampled composites being submitted for independent certified laboratory analysis."]},{"type":"p","children":["pXRF measurements and the confidence in the veracity of pXRF data based on its comparison with certified assays over the same core samples (announced on 2 September 2026) from the deposit, provides the opportunity for in-house derivation of both a geological model and the framework for a Mineral Resource Estimate which can be converted to a JORC (2012) Mineral Resource with the introduction of certified laboratory assays to replace pXRF estimates. The opportunity is being taken to define a geological model and generate an in-house volumetric estimate of mineralisation ahead of receipt of certified assays and the generation of a Mineral Resource."]},{"type":"p","children":["Highlights"]},{"type":"p","children":["·    pXRF drill results for RC and diamond drill holes targeting TK1 to TK7 sills and dykes at Teufelskuppe"]},{"type":"p","children":["·    Impressive continuous LREO grade and combined mineralised width intercepts including 5.08% over 20m, 4.85% over 23m, 4.30% over 15m, 4.28% over 26m, 3.37% over 40m, 3.36% over 48m and 3.27% over 46m"]},{"type":"p","children":["·    Peak LREO grades including 6.98% over 6.0m, 5.90% over 7.0m, 5.84% over 8.0m, 5.42% over 4.5m, 5.38% over 7.0m, 4.987% over 7.0m, 4.82% over 7.0m and 4.80% over 11m"]},{"type":"p","children":["·    Peak LREO mineralised widths with continuous grades of more than 2.0% LREO offering potential future bulk high-grade tonnage including 2.81% over 78m, 2.2% over 48.75m, 2.55% over 43m, 2.25% over 41m, 2.85% over 33m, 2.84% over 32m and 2.87% over 28m"]},{"type":"p","children":["·    LREO grade continuity through mineralised intercepts from top to bottom contact remains a defining characteristic of the TK deposit providing potential for a substantial tonnage to be defined"]},{"type":"p","children":["·    A total of 90 drill holes completed with further infill diamond drilling underway."]},{"type":"p","children":["Colin Bird, Chairman of Kendrick Resources, commented: \"The consistency of grade combined with excellent continuity of mineralisation over substantial widths remain the defining features of the Teufelskuppe deposit. With two drill rigs operating we are expanding our coverage over the multiple sills and dykes that make up the Teufelskuppe carbonatite complex. The pXRF data provides a high degree of confidence in the quality, distribution and grade of mineralisation and the regular inflow of certified assay results is confirming the credence of the data which will enable the development of a Mineral Resource Estimate\"."]},{"type":"p","children":["Table 1: pXRF Measurements for Teufelskuppe Diamond Drill Holes (TKDD019 to TKDD030) and RC Drill Holes (TKRC001 to TKRC20)"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-